<section class="sg-sec" id="inspired"><h2>What it inspired</h2><ul class="sg-chain"><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Second part of Lillibullero</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1688</span><span class="sg-chain-h">continuation</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A New Song Upon the Hogen Mogens</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1688</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody (anti-Dutch)</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">A New Irish Tune (Henry Purcell), Musick's Hand-Maid</span><span class="sg-chain-h">keyboard arrangement</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Marche du Prince d'Orange</span><span class="sg-chain-h">French version</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The Beggar's Opera (John Gay)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1728</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Tristram Shandy (Laurence Sterne)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">score printed in</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Piano Sonata No. 11 in A major, K. 331 (Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1783</span><span class="sg-chain-h">theme appears adapted from it</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Nottingham Ale</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">18th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Protestant Boys</span><span class="sg-chain-h">parody, same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">There Was an Old Woman Tossed Up in a Basket</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">19th century</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Overtures from Richmond (attributed to Francis J. Child)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">new words, same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Variations and Fugue on a Theme by Mozart, Op. 132 (Max Reger)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1914</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variations on the related theme</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Kleine Variationen über eine alt-irische Volksweise, Op. 146 (Walter Niemann)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1936</span><span class="sg-chain-h">variations</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">BBC World Service interval signal</span><span class="sg-chain-h">used as</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">The City Waites</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">1976</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording, with words of The Farmer's Curst Wife</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Bellowhead, Broadside</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2012</span><span class="sg-chain-h">recording, with words of The Farmer's Curst Wife</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Brown Bess (Rudyard Kipling, set by Michael Longcor)</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li><li><span class="sg-chain-n">Constitution Hill (Billy Bragg)</span> <span class="sg-chain-y">2009</span><span class="sg-chain-h">same melody</span></li></ul></section>
